WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.680
Best known to Pawn Stars fans as "The Old
Man," Richard Harrison passed away on Monday,

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:11.230
June 25th at the age of 77 after a battle
with Parkinson's disease.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:16.350
Harrison founded and operated the Las Vegas-based
World Famous Gold &amp; Silver Pawn Shop, which

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.350
he opened in 1989.

00:00:18.453 --> 00:00:22.452
Following his passing, the Pawn Stars team
paid tribute to Harrison, remembering the

00:00:22.452 --> 00:00:25.273
man he was and the work ethic he had.

00:00:25.273 --> 00:00:29.743
Harrison's son, Rick Harrison, for example,
shared two separate tributes to his father

00:00:29.743 --> 00:00:30.833
on Instagram.

00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:35.963
The first is a snap of the Old Man wearing
dark sunglasses and a fedora, with the touching

00:00:35.963 --> 00:00:37.642
caption that read in part:

00:00:37.642 --> 00:00:42.912
"He was my hero and I was fortunate to get
a very cool 'Old Man' as my dad.

00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:47.482
That I got to share him with so many others
and they got to see what a great family man

00:00:47.482 --> 00:00:51.623
he was is something I am grateful to have
experienced with him.

00:00:51.623 --> 00:00:56.093
He lived a very full life [...] touched the
lives of people all over, teaching them the

00:00:56.093 --> 00:00:59.543
value of loving your family, hard work, and
humor."

00:00:59.543 --> 00:01:03.923
Rick later posted a photo of his father from
his days in the U.S. Navy with the caption:

00:01:03.923 --> 00:01:08.933
"Today I lost a friend, a father, a teacher,
and so much more.

00:01:08.933 --> 00:01:12.263
The Old Man lost his long battle with Parkinson's
this morning.

00:01:12.263 --> 00:01:13.613
Love you Dad.

00:01:13.613 --> 00:01:14.613
See you on the other side."

00:01:14.613 --> 00:01:21.153
Similarly, Corey Harrison, also known as "Big
Hoss" to fans and family alike, remembered

00:01:21.153 --> 00:01:24.443
his grandfather as more than just a family
member.

00:01:24.443 --> 00:01:28.823
Harrison was more like a best friend to Corey,
who began helping out at the Gold &amp; Silver

00:01:28.823 --> 00:01:34.443
Pawn Shop when he was just 9 years old, later
becoming the store's full-time manager.

00:01:34.443 --> 00:01:39.083
In his own Instagram tribute, he shared a
younger Harrison wearing a suit and striped

00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:40.083
tie, writing:

00:01:40.083 --> 00:01:44.633
"I was lucky enough to spend 15 years of my
life working with the Old Man.

00:01:44.633 --> 00:01:48.623
He wasn't just a grandfather, he was truly
a best friend as well.

00:01:48.623 --> 00:01:51.403
I'm truly blessed to have had him as a mentor.

00:01:51.403 --> 00:01:53.063
He will be missed everyday."

00:01:53.063 --> 00:01:58.412
Corey's childhood friend and fellow shop worker
Austin "Chumlee" Russell also remembered Harrison

00:01:58.412 --> 00:02:03.503
as a kind, humorous man who offered honesty
and tough love when it mattered most.

00:02:03.503 --> 00:02:04.633
He wrote on Twitter:

00:02:04.633 --> 00:02:07.013
"It's hard to believe he is gone.

00:02:07.013 --> 00:02:10.802
He was such a big part of my life and treated
me like family.

00:02:10.802 --> 00:02:15.443
I will miss him greatly and carry the lessons
he taught me throughout my life.

00:02:15.443 --> 00:02:20.163
You could always count on him to straighten
you out or make you laugh and both of those

00:02:25.436 --> 00:02:29.466
a heartfelt tweet remembering their quirky
screen star by writing:

00:02:29.466 --> 00:02:35.356
"We are deeply saddened by the loss of our
friend Richard 'The Old Man' Harrison, a beloved

00:02:35.356 --> 00:02:38.086
member of the HISTORY and @pawnstars family.

00:02:38.086 --> 00:02:41.046
He will be greatly missed for his wisdom and
candor.

00:02:41.046 --> 00:02:44.336
Our thoughts are with the Harrison family
during this difficult time."

00:02:44.336 --> 00:02:48.726
The Gold &amp; Silver Pawn Shop Facebook page
also honored Harrison with a tribute that

00:02:48.726 --> 00:02:49.876
read, in part:

00:02:49.876 --> 00:02:54.326
"He will be remembered as the best father,
grandfather, and great-grandfather you could

00:02:54.326 --> 00:03:00.976
have by his family and by fans as the sometimes
grumpy (always loving, however), often wisecracking,

00:03:00.976 --> 00:03:05.316
and voice of absolute reason on the History
television show Pawn Stars."

00:03:05.316 --> 00:03:06.376
One thing's for sure.

